WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.766
Welcome to PixelVerse. I'll show you how to draw, animate, and share your own pixel art.

00:00:08.772 --> 00:00:16.356
Start on the canvas. Choose a colour, then click or drag to paint. Every pixel can be changed later.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:27.698
Try the pencil, eraser, fill, and picker. You can undo or redo a stroke any time.

00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:35.789
Duplicate a frame, change a few pixels, and use Onion Skin to see the previous one.

00:00:37.828 --> 00:00:43.684
Open View to show grid lines or Replay. Replay lets you watch your drawing come together.

00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:55.365
In PixelVerse Studio, preview your animation and adjust its speed. Then return to the canvas and open Create to make a pixel reference from an image.

00:00:57.383 --> 00:01:08.447
Choose Create from image, then select a picture. Set the resolution and number of colours, and press Convert to pixel art. The preview appears beside the original.

00:01:10.494 --> 00:01:17.046
When the preview looks right, use it as a reference. Open the reference panel and compare it with your drawing.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:24.642
Open Account to sign in with email or Google. You can still draw without an account.

00:01:26.661 --> 00:01:31.653
Save in your browser, export a project file, or keep your work in the cloud.

00:01:33.661 --> 00:01:39.061
Give your finished art a title, choose who can see it, and publish a fixed copy.

00:01:41.106 --> 00:01:46.578
Find artwork in the Gallery, save favourites, and react or leave a comment.

00:01:48.661 --> 00:01:54.661
Visit an artist's profile to see their public work. Follow them to catch their next creation.

00:01:56.661 --> 00:02:03.645
That's PixelVerse. Open the canvas and start creating. The Guide button is always there if you need it.
